  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Waste-to-Energy Facilities, through Government of Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $646,285 activity partially funds a feasibility study for the construction of two 24 MW waste-to-energy facilities in the Philippines. These facilities, projected to provide power to 64,000 homes, will assist the Philippines in meeting its renewable energy goals, as well as address energy shortfalls and increasing volumes of municipal solid waste. Bacavalley Energy Inc. is the grantee and Sinova Capital is the contractor and shares in the costs of the study.</narrative>
  </description>
